// #90, review round 4: a `&T` inside an annotation's array (or tuple) in a
// generic body is the `void **` a top-level one is, and a borrow of a concrete
// parameter meets it at no instantiation — refused by name.
//
// A generic body is not substituted, so `let r: [&T; 1] = [&a];` is `void
// **r[1] = {&a};` with `&a` a `long long *` at `T = i64`. Only a `&T` at the
// top of the annotation was asked. Measured on main (2ca5eb5) and on round 4
// alike: internal compiler error, the C backend emitted ill-typed C.
fn f<T>(a: T) -> i64 {
    let r: [&T; 1] = [&a];
    7
}

fn main() {
    print_int(f(5));
}
